OL,24,ANext Page BLondon NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,379,370,120,260,000,100
PN,37808
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F378A1785503911
OL,3,CSpeedboat killer admits assaulting
OL,4,Cpartner with barbecue tongs
OL,6,FThey had both been drinking champagne,
OL,7,Fand Shepherd handed the controls of
OL,8,Fthe boat to Ms Brown just before it
OL,9,Fstruck a submerged tree and
OL,10,Foverturned, tipping both of them into
OL,11,Fthe cold water.
OL,13,FHe was plucked from the Thames alive,
OL,14,Fbut Ms Brown was found unconscious and
OL,15,Funresponsive.
OL,17,FShepherd denied manslaughter by gross
OL,18,Fnegligence, but skipped the trial
OL,19,Fwhile on the run and did not give any
OL,20,Fevidence in his own defence.
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G8/9
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
